@startuml WoTA_UseCases
skinparam backgroundColor white
title WoTA co-working space API - base requirements
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
actor "Visitor" as visitor
actor "Registered user" as user
actor "Administrator" as admin
admin --|> user
rectangle "WoTA REST API" {
  usecase "Register account\nFR1" as register
  usecase "Sign in\nFR2" as login
  usecase "Sign out\nFR2" as logout
  usecase "Browse co-working rooms\nFR3" as browse
  usecase "Manage reservations\nFR3-FR9" as reservations
  usecase "Manage room catalogue\nPreserved Assignment 7 API" as rooms
}
visitor -- register
visitor -- login
visitor -- browse
user -- logout
user -- browse
user -- reservations
admin -- rooms
note right of reservations
  User: create up to 3 active reservations;
  view, edit and delete own reservations.
  Admin: view, edit and delete any reservation.
  Authentication is a precondition, not a sequence edge.
end note
note bottom of rooms
  Administrative room CRUD is preserved from the existing API.
  Additional requirements A1-A13 are documented separately.
end note
@enduml
